# Template for a new environment's committed, non-secret vars.
# Copy to .env.<mode> (one of: dev | staging | prod) and fill in the values.
# Committed file: NO secrets, NO personal/admin info (those live in .env.admin
# and .env.<mode>.secrets, both gitignored).
#
# Every key here must be UNIQUE across all four merged layers
# (.env.common + .env.<mode> + .env.admin + .env.<mode>.secrets); build-env
# ABORTS on any key defined in two layers. Put only what differs per environment
# here — shared defaults stay in .env.common.
#
# ENV is a per-environment label and does NOT change provisioning: CVM names are hardcoded
# `umbra-v0-*` regardless of ENV (routes.py / tee_provider/phala.py), so environment
# isolation comes from a dedicated Phala workspace/token (see .env.<mode>.secrets), NOT from ENV.
# LETSENCRYPT_STAGING picks the reverse-proxy CA:
# true = Let's Encrypt staging CA (untrusted certs, no rate limits; for dev/iteration),
# false = real CA (trusted certs; for prod and prod-like staging attestation).
ENV=
LETSENCRYPT_STAGING=
CONSOLE_HOST=
CONSOLE_URL=
VM_PUBLIC_IP=
UMBRA_CLI_WORKFLOW_BRANCH=
JWT_PRIVATE_KEY_REF=
JWT_ACTIVE_KID=
# Runtime publication targets. The supported publisher is GHCR-only; replace
# the reserved owner with namespaces you control before publishing.
SECURITY_CVM_IMAGE_REPOSITORY=ghcr.io/example/umbra-security-cvm
DEV_CVM_IMAGE_REPOSITORY=ghcr.io/example/umbra-dev-cvm
